Yes, I think I became first aware of that danger by your post at the 
time.  Since then I also have taken on the habit of destroying the 
drawbridge of the castle in order to avoid a stupid death...  If I ever 
cross it intact, I try to make sure no monster is around at all, because 
if there is one, it could have a wand of striking.

Now, concerning Lord Surtur's fortress, I figure that drawbridge deaths 
must be relatively frequent there, because it will often happen that 
when you kill a giant at the entrance, he will leave a boulder.  If you 
destroy that by a wand of striking while still on the bridge, you kill 
yourself (as I did, and I guess this does not happen more often than 
once to a player).  If you wait for another giant to pick it up, it 
might just happen that one of the giants inside has a wand of striking 
and fires it at you which is also deadly.  So the safest strategy in 
that case, too, is nuking the drawbridge from far away...  After all, a 
means of levitation or flying is compulsory when you do the valk quest 
(as well as fire resistance, I would say).
